          "source": "reviewer",
          "detail": "D1 [verdict ('Saturday included'); criteriaAssessments C4 assessment; edgeCasesAndFailureModes item 5 ('full 8-hour working day (Mon-Sat)'); rollout step 3 ('Berlin on-call working days (Mon-Sat)')] The text that was changed to fix the Saturday/s.9 problem now overreaches the other way. The verdict says call-outs 'on top of a normal working day, Saturday included, may exceed the s.3 daily ceiling'. C4 says 'On working days (Mon-Sat), call-outs on top of a normal 8-hour day could exceed the s.3 ceiling'. The draft's own working-hours assumption is 09:00-17:00 on weekdays only (K25-K30), so a Berlin engineer has no normal 8-hour day on Saturday. The 8 h + more than 2 h call-out breach scenario therefore applies Monday to Friday. On Saturday, s.3 is reached only by call-outs alone. The correct legal point is that s.3 covers Saturday and s.9 does not. Saying that Saturday call-outs sit on top of a normal workday overstates the Saturday s.3 risk."
        }
      ]
